  "answer_text": "The term **\"iCloud control\"** typically refers to one of three things depending on your operating system and what you are trying to achieve:\n\n---\n\n### 1. iCloud for Windows (Formerly \"iCloud Control Panel\")\nIf you are on a Windows PC, this is Apple's official software that allows you to sync and control your iCloud account features directly on Windows. \n\n* **What it does:**\n  * **iCloud Photos:** Syncs your photos and videos, making them available in the Microsoft Photos app.\n  * **iCloud Drive:** Access your cloud files directly inside Windows File Explorer.\n  * **iCloud Passwords:** Autofills your saved Keychain passwords using extensions in Google Chrome, Edge, or Firefox.\n  * **Contacts, Calendars, & Bookmarks:** Syncs your Apple calendars/contacts to classic Outlook and bookmarks to your preferred PC browser.\n* **How to get it:** You can download it for free directly from the **Microsoft Store** (search for \"iCloud\").\n\n---\n\n### 2. \"iCloud-Control\" (Third-Party macOS Utility)\nIf you are on a Mac, **iCloud-Control** is a well-known, free open-source utility (originally hosted on GitHub).\n\n* **What it does:** It adds an icon/menu to macOS Finder that allows for **selective synchronization** of iCloud Drive. It gives you the ability to manually \"evict\" (remove the local copy of a file/folder to save space) or force-download files on command.\n* *Note:* The original developer officially discontinued the project in 2024, as modern versions of macOS (Sonoma and newer) have built-in Finder controls for managing iCloud storage. However, the tool is still used by legacy Mac users or can be installed via Homebrew using `brew install --cask icloud-control`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Native iCloud Controls (iOS, Mac, and Web)\nIf you are looking to manage, view, or control your iCloud storage and sync settings natively on your Apple devices:\n\n* **On iPhone, iPad, or Apple Vision Pro:**\n  1. Open the **Settings** app.\n  2. Tap **your name** (Apple ID / Account) at the top of the screen.\n  3. Tap **iCloud**. Here you can toggle which apps sync to the cloud and manage your storage.\n* **On Mac:**\n  1. Go to the Apple menu (\uf8ff) > **System Settings**.\n  2. Click **your name** at the top of the sidebar.\n  3. Click **iCloud** on the right side to manage sync settings and storage.\n* **On the Web:**\n  * You can log into **[iCloud.com](https://www.icloud.com)** from any device to view, download, or delete emails, photos, notes, and drive files.\n\n***\n\n**Which of these were you looking for?** If you have a specific goal (such as freeing up iCloud storage, setting up parental controls, or syncing files), let me know and I can provide step-by-step instructions!",
